CREATE TABLE results_database.id_first_occurrence
WITH (
    format='PARQUET',
    parquet_compression='SNAPPY',
    external_location='s3://your-output-bucket/id-first-occurrence/'
) AS
SELECT
    id,
    CAST(FLOOR(MIN(yr*4+qtr-1)/4) AS INTEGER) AS first_yr,
    CAST(MOD(MIN(yr*4+qtr-1),4)+1 AS INTEGER) AS first_qtr,
    CONCAT(
        CAST(CAST(FLOOR(MIN(yr*4+qtr-1)/4) AS INTEGER) AS VARCHAR),
        '-Q',
        CAST(CAST(MOD(MIN(yr*4+qtr-1),4)+1 AS INTEGER) AS VARCHAR)
    ) AS first_yr_qtr
FROM source_database.parquet_table
WHERE id IS NOT NULL
  AND TRIM(id)<>''
  AND yr IS NOT NULL
  AND qtr BETWEEN 1 AND 4
GROUP BY id;


Use Amazon Athena because this calculation only needs to run once.
Create an AWS Glue Crawler pointed at the S3 folder containing the Parquet files.
Run the crawler to create a Glue Data Catalog table containing the ID, year, and quarter columns.
Open Amazon Athena and select the Glue database created for the Parquet table.
Configure a separate S3 folder for Athena’s query results.
Run a CREATE TABLE AS SELECT query that groups the records by ID and finds the earliest year-quarter for each ID.
Save the resulting table as compressed Parquet in a new, empty S3 output folder.
Query the new Athena table to verify that it contains one row per ID with its first year and quarter.
